"comparison": "Both NVDA and Broadcom (AVGO) disclose that the timing of new product introductions and customer deployments creates significant revenue volatility and forecasting challenges. NVDA specifically cites that 'Qualification time for new products, customers anticipating product transitions and channel partners reducing channel inventory of prior architectures ahead of new product introductions can create reductions or volatility in our revenue.' Similarly, AVGO states that for its AI and wireless products, 'fluctuations may be magnified by the timing of customer deployments and product launches, and seasonal variations in sales.' Both companies identify the synchronization between product launch cadence and customer adoption/deployment as a key driver of revenue unpredictability.",
