"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Intel (INTC) mirrors NVDA's disclosure regarding the operational risks inherent in complex product and technology transitions. NVDA states that 'Deployment of new products to customers creates additional challenges due to the complexity of our technologies... [and] may impair our ability to predict demand.' INTC similarly highlights that 'Forecasting our progress and schedule for developing advanced nodes and other technologies is challenging, and at times we encounter unexpected delays due to the complexity of interactions among steps in the manufacturing process.' Both companies explicitly link technical complexity during transitions to difficulties in accurate demand or schedule forecasting and potential delays.",
